{"ukmt-tmc-2025-national-crossnumber-01":[{"title":"Solution","body":"- Fibonacci clues: the 4-digit multiple of 5 is $6765$ (8A); the Fibonacci number before it is $4181$ (7D); 12D is the 4-digit Fibonacci multiple of 37: $4181=37\\times113$ (12D $=4181$), so 19A $=2584$ and 4A $=37$.\n- 13A $=314$ ($314^2=98596$). 9A and 16D: 16D is the mean of 9A and 16D, which forces 16D $=$ 9A $=125$ (the cube in the grid). 15D: two-digit factor of $1111$ is $11$, so $11^3=1331$. 23D: $6765=3\\cdot5\\cdot11\\cdot41$, so $41$. 6A: $(41-1)/4=10$ sides, angle $144$. \n- 20D is a square, $841$, and 11A (the mean of 20D and 11A) equals 20D, so 11A $=841$. 21A is the multiple of 9 $135$; 6D: $135/9=15$ sides gives $156$. 22D: $\\sqrt{125^2-120^2}=35$.\n- 10A: $16\\text{D}+18=143$, $16\\text{D}+20=145$, so the shortest side is $\\sqrt{145^2-143^2}=24$. 17A $=360-125-156-41=38$. 1D $=360-125-135-24=76$. 3D $=\\sqrt{4\\times144}=24$ (6A $=144$).\n- 5D: $841+135+(2\\times39)^2-10=7050$; 14D, 2D and 8D, 18A, 25A follow: 1A $=\\frac32\\times4181+\\frac12(1331+434)=7154$; 14D $=434$; 2D $=527$ (528 is triangular); 8D $=648$; 18A $=378$ ($=27\\cdot28/2$); 24A: sixth column digits $2,4,3,5,1$ sum to $15$; 25A $=1111$.\n\nCompleted answers: Across: 1: 7154, 4: 37, 6: 144, 8: 6765, 9: 125, 10: 24, 11: 841, 13: 314, 17: 38, 18: 378, 19: 2584, 21: 135, 24: 15, 25: 1111. Down: 1: 76, 2: 527, 3: 24, 5: 7050, 6: 156, 7: 4181, 8: 648, 12: 4181, 14: 434, 15: 1331, 16: 125, 20: 841, 22: 35, 23: 41.\n\n**Answer: the completed grid above.**"}]}